1
00:01:20,421 --> 00:01:21,985
بِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمَانِ الرَّحِيْمَ۝

2
00:01:22,604 --> 00:01:29,277
اَلْحَمْدُ لله ، وَالصَّلَاةُ وَالسَّلَامُ عَلى سَيِّدِنَا محمد وَعَلَى اَلِهِ وَصَحْبِهِ وَسَلِّمْ تَسْلِيْمًا كَثِيْراً

3
00:01:33,285 --> 00:01:34,808
This evening we'll talk about,

4
00:01:36,107 --> 00:01:42,893
the rules of Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) in choosing his governors.

5
00:01:45,597 --> 00:01:55,309
These are the men, who would face the people and represent Umar(عُمَر) in the various Muslim states.

6
00:01:58,331 --> 00:02:04,147
In those days it would be impossible to have a centralized system.

7
00:02:05,919 --> 00:02:10,595
So, it was more of a federal system,

8
00:02:11,958 --> 00:02:19,616
where the Muslim Khilafah(خِلَافَه) is divided into states, Wilayaat(ولايات)

9
00:02:20,711 --> 00:02:23,658
and every state is headed by a governor,

10
00:02:24,490 --> 00:02:28,782
and that Governor has a lot of independence.

11
00:02:30,575 --> 00:02:39,401
Because keep in mind that in those days, there was no telephone service, no fax service, no email

12
00:02:41,366 --> 00:02:48,152
forms of transportation were very slow, no planes, no cars, no trains.

13
00:02:49,335 --> 00:02:56,519
So it's impossible to have a centralized system, where everything is controlled from Madina.

14
00:02:58,445 --> 00:03:05,294
Therefore the choice of Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) of governors was very important

15
00:03:06,413 --> 00:03:14,904
because these will be his representatives in establishing the law of Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ.

16
00:03:17,439 --> 00:03:26,082
So, what were the qualities that he was looking for, when he would choose a Waali(والي).

17
00:03:28,606 --> 00:03:35,463
Now, the posts that existed then, was Waali(والي)

18
00:03:36,352 --> 00:03:42,182
and then you have a Ameer Al-Jund(اميرالجند), this is the military general,

19
00:03:42,563 --> 00:03:44,682
you had Qaadhi(قاضي), judge

20
00:03:45,666 --> 00:03:50,427
and you had Aamil Zaka'ah(عامل زكواة), the one who collects the Zakaah(زكوة).

21
00:03:51,083 --> 00:03:55,611
Sometimes these roles would be in Independent and sometimes they would be combined.

22
00:03:58,727 --> 00:04:04,754
Number one, Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) was searching for Al-Qawwi-Ul-Ameen(القوى الامين).

23
00:04:05,794 --> 00:04:08,544
Al-Qawwi(القوي) the literal translation of it is strong

24
00:04:08,569 --> 00:04:12,729
but I think we talked about this concept earlier that it really means the competent,

25
00:04:13,510 --> 00:04:16,170
somebody who's competent in that field.

26
00:04:18,254 --> 00:04:20,754
It doesn't necessarily mean physical strength

27
00:04:21,375 --> 00:04:23,701
it means that you are strong in that field

28
00:04:26,080 --> 00:04:30,313
and also Amanah(امانة), the person needs to be trust worthy.

29
00:04:32,221 --> 00:04:38,066
Shurhabeel Bin Hasanah(شُرحبيل بن حسنة), one of the Umara'a(امراء)

30
00:04:40,254 --> 00:04:42,341
was changed by Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب)

31
00:04:44,122 --> 00:04:49,244
and he appointed instead of him Muawiyah Bin abi Sufiyan(معاويه بن ابي سفيان).

32
00:04:51,497 --> 00:04:54,155
So, Sharhabeel(شُرحبيل) went to Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) and he said;

33
00:04:55,441 --> 00:04:58,885
Did you change me because I've done something wrong? You're upset with me?

34
00:04:59,458 --> 00:05:01,505
I've angered you in one way or another?

35
00:05:01,947 --> 00:05:04,669
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) said: No! That's not the reason.

36
00:05:05,009 --> 00:05:07,083
وَإِنَّمَا رَجُلٌ اَقْوَى مِنْ رَّجُلْ

37
00:05:07,416 --> 00:05:11,320
But because, there is a man who's stronger than another man.

38
00:05:12,530 --> 00:05:14,709
So, the reason why I changed you is because I think

39
00:05:14,734 --> 00:05:19,929
that Muawiyah Bin abi Sufiyan(معاويه بن ابي سفيان) is more capable of fulfilling this particular role.

40
00:05:22,477 --> 00:05:24,993
Shurhabeel Bin Hasanah(شُرحبيل بن حسنة), was a good the military leader.

41
00:05:25,018 --> 00:05:32,343
He was appointed in the time of Abu Bakr Siddique رضي الله عنه to lead one of the armies that were in Ash-sham(ألشام).

42
00:05:33,006 --> 00:05:37,480
But in this particular post now, there might have been a civilian post, role.

43
00:05:37,951 --> 00:05:40,962
He was changed and Muawiya(معاويه) replaced him

44
00:05:41,240 --> 00:05:44,299
and Umar رضي الله عنه, gave the justification. He said;

45
00:05:44,324 --> 00:05:45,581
"رَجُلٌ اَقْوَى مِنْ رَّجُلْ"

46
00:05:46,016 --> 00:05:47,883
Some men are stronger than others.

47
00:05:49,314 --> 00:05:55,506
In fact, there is another story that Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) was asking, he said;

48
00:05:56,767 --> 00:06:02,971
Who is better Mo'min Muttaqi(مؤمن متقي) who has Taqwa(تقوى), but is weak

49
00:06:04,098 --> 00:06:07,243
 or somebody, who is strong.

50
00:06:09,335 --> 00:06:12,076
So, the response Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) got was,

51
00:06:14,183 --> 00:06:16,985
 the Taqwa(تقوى) of the Muslim is for himself,

52
00:06:17,189 --> 00:06:20,956
but his weakness would affect his subjects.

53
00:06:22,584 --> 00:06:28,464
While the strength of a man would affect his subjects positively.

54
00:06:28,922 --> 00:06:32,001
So, they're telling him that appointing somebody, who's strong

55
00:06:33,469 --> 00:06:37,140
but might have less Taqwa(تقوى) than somebody else, who's weak is better.

56
00:06:40,047 --> 00:06:43,559
Now, obviously we're talking about here relative scale of Taqwa(تقوى).

57
00:06:43,584 --> 00:06:47,617
We're not talking about somebody who is Fasiq(فاسق) both have Taqwa(تقوى)

58
00:06:48,361 --> 00:06:50,777
but one of them has more Taqwa(تقوى) than the other.

59
00:06:52,718 --> 00:06:57,448
There has to be a bottom line of Taqwa(تقوى) with anybody who assumes a position of leadership.

60
00:06:57,806 --> 00:06:58,812
 No matter what it is!.

61
00:07:01,955 --> 00:07:03,814
Umar Bin Khattab رضي الله عنه used to say;

62
00:07:03,838 --> 00:07:09,966
اَللَّهُمَّ اِنِّيْ أَشْقُوْ عَلَيْكَ ,عَجْزِلْ مُؤْمِنْ, وَجَلَدِالْكَافِرْ

63
00:07:11,719 --> 00:07:23,119
"O Allah I seek refuge in You from a strong disbeliever and a weak or incapable believer."

64
00:07:26,089 --> 00:07:28,491
I seek refuge in you, from a Kafir(كافر) who is  strong.

65
00:07:29,504 --> 00:07:32,100
A Kafir(كافر) who's devoted to serving Shaytan(شَيْطَانْ).

66
00:07:33,766 --> 00:07:36,051
Who sleeps very little and works a lot.

67
00:07:37,429 --> 00:07:40,348
And I seek refuge in You, from a believer who's doing nothing.

68
00:07:45,401 --> 00:07:47,243
So, make sure that you are not one of those

69
00:07:47,267 --> 00:07:50,986
whom Umar Bin Khattab رضي الله عنه is seeking refuge in Allah from.

70
00:07:53,084 --> 00:08:03,405
It doesn't make sense to have a believer who knows the truth,

71
00:08:04,038 --> 00:08:06,092
who has who has Baseerah(بصيره), who has seen the light,

72
00:08:07,280 --> 00:08:10,335
who knows about Jannah(جنة), who knows about Hellfire

73
00:08:11,282 --> 00:08:14,123
sitting down and doing nothing, a couch potato.

74
00:08:15,699 --> 00:08:20,777
And then you have a Kafir(كافر) who's blind, blinded from the truth

75
00:08:21,730 --> 00:08:23,913
and knows nothing about the path of Shaytan(شَيْطَانْ)

76
00:08:24,558 --> 00:08:27,516
and is devoted and active and hard working.

77
00:08:30,118 --> 00:08:34,490
How can the soldier of Shaytan(شَيْطَانْ) be better than the soldier of Ar-Rahman(الرحمن)

78
00:08:36,901 --> 00:08:39,095
it's a shame if that's the case.

79
00:08:41,753 --> 00:08:44,934
So, make sure brother and sister that you're not one of those,

80
00:08:46,073 --> 00:08:50,452
because Jibreel عليه السّلام, he came to Muhammadﷺ and said;

81
00:08:50,651 --> 00:08:51,029
"عَجِبْتُ"

82
00:08:51,054 --> 00:08:53,277
I am surprised.

83
00:08:53,523 --> 00:08:56,206
 Jibreel(جِبْرِيْل) is telling Muhammadﷺ, I am surprised

84
00:08:56,472 --> 00:09:02,499
how can somebody know about Jannah(جنة) and then not work for it?

85
00:09:03,394 --> 00:09:09,361
And how can somebody know about Hellfire and then sleep and not seek refuge from it?

86
00:09:10,277 --> 00:09:11,232
How could that be?

87
00:09:16,589 --> 00:09:20,937
Rasool Allah ﷺ says: On the Day of Judgment

88
00:09:23,059 --> 00:09:26,251
if there was a person who was being pulled on his face in Duniyah(دُنِيَّا),

89
00:09:26,275 --> 00:09:30,079
I mean imagine, being pulled on your face.

90
00:09:30,759 --> 00:09:34,750
Right! You're being dragged by a car on your face,

91
00:09:35,111 --> 00:09:37,294
since the day you were born until the day you die.

92
00:09:37,939 --> 00:09:44,327
Rasool Allah ﷺ said: If there was somebody who was being pulled on their face, in Duniyah(دُنِيَّا),

93
00:09:45,046 --> 00:09:48,932
from the day they were born, until the day they were they died,

94
00:09:49,790 --> 00:09:54,495
they would see that as insignificant on the day of judgment, when they face Allah.

95
00:09:56,376 --> 00:10:02,822
If you suffered your entire life in the sake of Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ by being dragged on your face,

96
00:10:02,847 --> 00:10:05,907
 suffering that torment, day in and day out.

97
00:10:06,243 --> 00:10:10,812
On the Day of Judgment, when you see the reality you would view.

98
00:10:11,094 --> 00:10:14,439
What was done to you as insignificant? Nothing.!

99
00:10:18,657 --> 00:10:24,055
لَيْسَ يَتَحَسَّرُ أَهْلُ الْجَنَّةِ إِلا عَلَى سَاعَةٍ مَرَّتْ بِهِمْ لا يَذْكُرُونَ اللَّهَ عَزَّ وَجَلَّ فِيهَا

100
00:10:24,559 --> 00:10:29,485
" the people of Jannah(جنة) don't regret anything but a moment that passed by them and Duniyah(دُنِيَّا)

101
00:10:29,525 --> 00:10:31,658
 and they didn't mention the name of Allah."

102
00:10:36,285 --> 00:10:37,440
Number two,

103
00:10:39,228 --> 00:10:40,324
اَلْبَصَرْ بِالْعَمَلْ

104
00:10:40,419 --> 00:10:44,419
Experience! He was looking for experience.

105
00:10:46,147 --> 00:10:51,027
He was about to assign someone to the post of a Waali(الوالي),

106
00:10:52,789 --> 00:10:59,466
and then they told Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) and apparently they told him, this as a praise of this man

107
00:10:59,633 --> 00:11:01,860
they said this man knows no evil,

108
00:11:03,402 --> 00:11:06,543
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) said: If he doesn't know evil, then he might commit it.

109
00:11:07,918 --> 00:11:10,897
And he refused to assign him to that post.

110
00:11:15,029 --> 00:11:18,861
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) wanted a man who was experienced,

111
00:11:20,467 --> 00:11:22,975
who knows about Ash-Shar(الشر), knows about evil,

112
00:11:23,340 --> 00:11:26,337
because if you know about it, you won't fall into it.

113
00:11:28,661 --> 00:11:31,657
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) was not interested in finding,

114
00:11:33,388 --> 00:11:37,973
what we would call today, a nerd or a bookworm, who's sitting at home, studying the books,

115
00:11:38,320 --> 00:11:40,106
you know, doing all of the Shariah Ilm(شريعه علم),

116
00:11:40,333 --> 00:11:43,005
 but doesn't know what's going on in the streets.

117
00:11:44,327 --> 00:11:50,051
Because such a person would be inexperienced, he would be shocked by reality.

118
00:11:50,515 --> 00:11:52,785
He has an ideal view of the world.

119
00:11:54,264 --> 00:11:57,613
But Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) wants, people who,

120
00:11:58,202 --> 00:12:01,230
in fact, in one statement Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) said;

121
00:12:01,571 --> 00:12:08,838
Islam will be lost when there will be people, who don't know about Jahilliyah(جاهلية).

122
00:12:12,515 --> 00:12:15,211
He said: These generations that are being born in Islam

123
00:12:16,006 --> 00:12:18,826
and they know nothing about the slam, they don't know Jahilliyah(جاهلية),

124
00:12:19,486 --> 00:12:22,146
they are the ones, who would lose Islam.

125
00:12:23,314 --> 00:12:28,332
Why? Because they don't know the bitter taste of Jahilliyah(جاهلية), they haven't tasted it.

126
00:12:31,936 --> 00:12:33,796
لَيْسَ الْخَبَرْالكَلْ مُعَيْنَا

127
00:12:33,820 --> 00:12:36,143
 Hearing about something is not like seeing it.

128
00:12:37,324 --> 00:12:39,043
We can read about Jahilliyah(جاهلية).

129
00:12:39,607 --> 00:12:44,688
But the ones who lived Jahilliyah(جاهلية), they're the ones who really, really, really hate it.

130
00:12:46,626 --> 00:12:53,802
And that's why you would find that, an ex smoker hates the smell of cigarettes

131
00:12:54,076 --> 00:12:56,747
more than someone who never smoked in his life.

132
00:12:58,693 --> 00:13:04,194
The smokers will testify to that, you just can't stand that smell anymore.

133
00:13:05,250 --> 00:13:09,304
And I would assume maybe the same could be said about people who were former alcoholics

134
00:13:09,329 --> 00:13:13,219
Allah Ho Alam(الله أعلم), maybe because alcohol is different maybe sometimes

135
00:13:13,453 --> 00:13:17,590
the person could have that maybe with alcohol and drugs,

136
00:13:17,953 --> 00:13:21,777
unless a person is very, very, very detached from it.

137
00:13:22,016 --> 00:13:25,882
Maybe they could still have that addiction attachment to it, Allah Ho Alam(الله أعلم),

138
00:13:27,112 --> 00:13:33,422
but the thing is here that, with the Sahabah رضي الله عنهم, who grew up in Shirk(شرك)

139
00:13:36,495 --> 00:13:41,224
for them Islam was everything, because Islam saved them.

140
00:13:42,185 --> 00:13:44,918
But  somebody, who was born into it, might take it for granted.

141
00:13:47,818 --> 00:13:49,416
So, Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) is saying;

142
00:13:51,109 --> 00:13:52,572
اَحْرَهْ اَيْنَ يَقَعَأ فِيْ

143
00:13:52,953 --> 00:13:57,781
If he doesn't know about Sharr(شر) if he doesn't know evil, he might be tricked into it.

144
00:14:01,018 --> 00:14:03,709
So, Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) is looking for people who are experienced

145
00:14:03,838 --> 00:14:08,799
people who cannot be tricked, who cannot be fooled, people who are not naive or gullible,

146
00:14:09,963 --> 00:14:13,924
people who know the haqq(حقّ) and they know the Batil(باطل) and you cannot fool them.

147
00:14:24,447 --> 00:14:30,746
Number three: And this was one of the conditions, he would never appoint a relative

148
00:14:32,994 --> 00:14:35,100
even if they were qualified,

149
00:14:36,581 --> 00:14:39,957
one of the most qualified man among the Sahabah(صحابه) was, Abdullah Ibn Umar(عبدالله ابن عمر)

150
00:14:41,526 --> 00:14:45,166
and his name was brought up in many nominations

151
00:14:46,162 --> 00:14:48,694
and Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) would respond to them harshly.

152
00:14:50,405 --> 00:14:53,861
Once he said: I want a man who has these qualities 1,2,3…..

153
00:14:54,139 --> 00:14:55,420
The man said that I have him.

154
00:14:57,030 --> 00:15:00,487
I know who should, who that man is, Umar(عُمَر) said: Who?

155
00:15:00,794 --> 00:15:02,359
He said: Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب). He said;

156
00:15:02,443 --> 00:15:04,718
قَاتَلَكَ اللهَ مَا أَرَتْ بِذَالِكَ وَجْه’ الله

157
00:15:05,305 --> 00:15:09,351
 May Allah kill you, you don't want the face of Allah with that statement.

158
00:15:11,457 --> 00:15:12,721
 you just want to make me happy.

159
00:15:15,159 --> 00:15:17,780
Even though the man might have been very sincere, in that suggestion.

160
00:15:20,543 --> 00:15:27,636
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) ruled out having any of his family assume positions of responsibility.

161
00:15:28,429 --> 00:15:30,971
And the most beloved of his family to him, was Abdullah(عبدالله)

162
00:15:32,592 --> 00:15:34,081
and he would tell his son;

163
00:15:34,470 --> 00:15:38,668
O my son, it's enough for one of us,

164
00:15:39,879 --> 00:15:43,419
to be trialed on the Day of Judgment for being responsible for the Muslims.

165
00:15:45,755 --> 00:15:48,064
It's enough for one man from the family of Umar(عُمَر)

166
00:15:48,544 --> 00:15:52,809
to be held accountable on the Day of Judgment for everything that happens to every Muslim.

167
00:15:53,568 --> 00:15:58,967
I don't want anyone else of my family to suffer that on the Day of Judgment.

168
00:16:00,174 --> 00:16:10,261
He viewed it as a responsibility that he would be asked about, he would say;

169
00:16:12,231 --> 00:16:19,906
مَنِسْتَعْمَلَ رَجُلً لِمَوَدَّةْ أَوْ قَرَابَهْ لَا يَشْغَلُه’ إِلَّا ذَالِكْ فَقَدْ خَائِنَاللهَ وَرَسُوْلَه’

170
00:16:20,513 --> 00:16:29,887
If someone appoints a relative or a friend for no reason, but their relationship or friendship,

171
00:16:30,391 --> 00:16:33,102
they have betrayed Allah and His Messenger.

172
00:16:34,844 --> 00:16:37,806
If you appoint a relative or you appoint a friend.

173
00:16:38,614 --> 00:16:42,711
And the reason why you do so, is because they are your friend or relative,

174
00:16:43,262 --> 00:16:47,583
then that is betraying Allah and His messenger.

175
00:16:48,859 --> 00:16:53,871
So, in our organizations in our Masajid(مساجد) it in our Islamic groups,

176
00:16:54,070 --> 00:16:57,966
we need to make sure that the reason why we are appointing people,

177
00:16:58,322 --> 00:17:01,697
is not because they're from the same tribe, from the same clan,

178
00:17:01,939 --> 00:17:04,385
from the same family, because he's my buddy.

179
00:17:06,400 --> 00:17:11,945
They should be chosen based on the merits, based on their qualifications,

180
00:17:12,651 --> 00:17:14,121
because this is an Amanah(أمانة).

181
00:17:15,699 --> 00:17:23,552
And a person who appoints somebody is, as the person who's responsible.

182
00:17:32,073 --> 00:17:39,802
Number four: He would never appoint somebody who asked for it.

183
00:17:41,605 --> 00:17:48,567
If he feels that somebody is seeking that position of responsibility,

184
00:17:48,974 --> 00:17:52,236
somebody who is power hungry, he would avoid him.

185
00:17:54,250 --> 00:17:59,773
He would not give it to somebody who is keen to have that responsibility

186
00:18:00,906 --> 00:18:02,046
because, he would say;

187
00:18:02,289 --> 00:18:06,808
مَنْ يَطْلُبُ هَذَا لْأَمْرَلَمْ يُعَنْ عَلَيْهََ

188
00:18:08,809 --> 00:18:14,002
Whoever asks for this affair would not be supported by Allah in it.

189
00:18:15,730 --> 00:18:23,416
If a person is appointed in a position of responsibility, then Allah will help that person

190
00:18:24,358 --> 00:18:31,420
but if a person asked for it, and struggles to get it then Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ will leave that person alone

191
00:18:33,400 --> 00:18:37,843
and in such positions of responsibility, you definitely need the help of Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ.

192
00:18:37,868 --> 00:18:39,323
You don't want to be left on your own.

193
00:18:40,890 --> 00:18:43,366
So, somebody who asked for it will not be held by Allah

194
00:18:43,391 --> 00:18:45,534
while somebody who does not ask for it.

195
00:18:46,788 --> 00:18:49,671
And it doesn't make a difference to that person, whether their appointed or not,

196
00:18:49,836 --> 00:18:53,642
such a person will be given help and assistance by Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ.

197
00:19:00,668 --> 00:19:08,453
Number six. And this is an interesting condition. 1, 2, 3, 4, 5,

198
00:19:12,251 --> 00:19:21,721
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) would ban anyone who is in a position of responsibility

199
00:19:22,094 --> 00:19:27,876
 from being involved in trade or commerce.

200
00:19:30,050 --> 00:19:34,283
If a person is a Waali(وآلي), they are not allowed to do business,

201
00:19:36,726 --> 00:19:42,707
he would give them a good salary, but they would not be allowed to invest any money

202
00:19:42,992 --> 00:19:46,029
and get involved in business.

203
00:19:47,651 --> 00:19:51,333
And Ibn Khaldoon(ابن خلدون) he talks about this concept in his book in Al-Muqaddamah(المقدمه).

204
00:19:52,643 --> 00:19:55,950
And he has a long essay about this.

205
00:19:56,777 --> 00:20:03,779
And what he's saying is that whenever you have a mixture of political leadership

206
00:20:04,304 --> 00:20:07,792
and business, business goes wrong.

207
00:20:10,265 --> 00:20:15,190
When somebody who has political power gets involved in business,

208
00:20:15,916 --> 00:20:21,029
they would have an edge over the businessmen who are not politicians.

209
00:20:22,384 --> 00:20:28,226
And that is a flaw in the equilibrium that exists in the market.

210
00:20:28,418 --> 00:20:34,477
You see, Islam allows the people to do business

211
00:20:34,501 --> 00:20:38,350
without placing any restrictions on them except the restrictions of Shariah(شريعه).

212
00:20:39,372 --> 00:20:41,650
For example, when the prices went up in Al-Madina(المدينه)

213
00:20:43,138 --> 00:20:45,809
they came to Rasool Allah ﷺ and said: O Rasool Ullah

214
00:20:46,107 --> 00:20:46,887
سَائِرْلَنَا

215
00:20:46,911 --> 00:20:53,656
O Rasool Ullah make a pricing for us, to reduce the prices.

216
00:20:54,006 --> 00:20:54,971
Rasool Allah ﷺ said;

217
00:20:55,291 --> 00:20:57,052
إِنَّ اللهَ هُوَالْمُسَائِرْ

218
00:20:57,471 --> 00:21:03,405
Allah is the One, Who sets the prices and He is the One, Who gives Ar-Rizq(الرزق)

219
00:21:03,957 --> 00:21:07,676
and I don't want to be held accountable on the Day of Judgment

220
00:21:08,164 --> 00:21:11,075
for preventing the Ar-Rizq(الرزق) of someone from getting to him.

221
00:21:12,417 --> 00:21:15,311
Rasool Allah ﷺ is saying: There's a certain equilibrium in the market.

222
00:21:16,596 --> 00:21:19,338
And that equilibrium is what, determines the prices

223
00:21:19,666 --> 00:21:22,235
it's a supply and demand thing, that's what they say today.

224
00:21:23,213 --> 00:21:26,280
Even though that's not how it was expressed in the Hadith(حديث) of Rasool Allah ﷺ

225
00:21:26,305 --> 00:21:27,465
but it is the same concept.

226
00:21:28,156 --> 00:21:30,422
It is Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ who sets the prices.

227
00:21:31,115 --> 00:21:32,972
Based on the supply and demand in the market

228
00:21:32,996 --> 00:21:35,286
Somtimes the prices would go up sometimes, they would go down.

229
00:21:35,687 --> 00:21:42,751
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ is saying: I don't want to intervene myself and set or fix the prices

230
00:21:43,284 --> 00:21:47,416
 because I would be committing oppression, wrong against someone

231
00:21:48,407 --> 00:21:51,586
either the buyer or the seller, I would be wronging in one of them.

232
00:21:56,329 --> 00:22:00,675
However, when somebody who has political power gets involved in business

233
00:22:00,723 --> 00:22:04,813
 because of that upper hand

234
00:22:06,908 --> 00:22:11,373
that is an advantage for that person and the marketplace,

235
00:22:13,025 --> 00:22:16,545
you would find disadvantage with everybody else.

236
00:22:17,528 --> 00:22:21,516
And Ibn Khaldoon(ابن خلدون)  says: That causes Fasad(فساد), it causes corruption.

237
00:22:23,059 --> 00:22:27,689
So, he said that the Sultan(سلطان) and all of his workers employees

238
00:22:28,161 --> 00:22:31,660
need to pull their hands out of business completely

239
00:22:32,663 --> 00:22:37,229
and they should be paid by the Muslim Treasury a salary that is sufficient for them

240
00:22:37,538 --> 00:22:41,984
and they should not be allowed to intervene in business whatsoever.

241
00:22:42,798 --> 00:22:45,240
Politicians should be separate from businessmen

242
00:22:46,954 --> 00:22:53,181
and that was something that Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) has stated centuries before Ibn Khaldoon(ابن خلدون).

243
00:22:55,048 --> 00:23:00,409
His Ummal(عمال) and Wulaa(ولآه) were prevented from doing business.

244
00:23:05,651 --> 00:23:06,651
Number Six;

245
00:23:11,040 --> 00:23:14,721
To make sure that this rule is applied,

246
00:23:16,166 --> 00:23:28,584
he would make an accounting of the wealth of the Waali(وآلي) before the appointment

247
00:23:29,659 --> 00:23:34,756
and when he is discharged from his job.

248
00:23:36,755 --> 00:23:42,961
So, he would make Muhasibah(محاسبه) accounting of every single penny that, this Waali(وآلي) has.

249
00:23:44,091 --> 00:23:45,486
For example Muadh Ibn Jabal(معاذابن جبل)

250
00:23:45,952 --> 00:23:49,241
he would look at the wealth of Muadh Ibn Jabal(معاذابن جبل) how much does he have?

251
00:23:50,499 --> 00:23:56,840
And then when he is discharged from that job, he would hold him accountable again.

252
00:23:58,514 --> 00:24:03,541
Any plus, any surplus that the Waali(وآلي) would have

253
00:24:04,467 --> 00:24:05,954
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) would take it away.

254
00:24:07,874 --> 00:24:11,026
If he had 100,000 before he became Waali(وآلي)

255
00:24:12,344 --> 00:24:16,020
and then after he is discharged, he has 150,

256
00:24:16,258 --> 00:24:19,144
he would take that 50,000 and put it in Bait Ul-Maal(بيت المال).

257
00:24:20,705 --> 00:24:22,456
Therefore according to Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب)

258
00:24:23,847 --> 00:24:26,543
you're not supposed to leave your job with more money.

259
00:24:29,378 --> 00:24:32,349
We pay your salary to make a living during that time and that's it.

260
00:24:32,615 --> 00:24:34,436
You are not supposed to walk out as a millionaire.

261
00:24:39,347 --> 00:24:46,692
In fact, it is said that he would command his Wulaa(ولاء) to come into Madina during daytime

262
00:24:47,311 --> 00:24:49,713
 and not at night, so that they can't hide anything.

263
00:24:56,564 --> 00:24:57,359
Number seven;

264
00:24:59,422 --> 00:25:03,300
He would have them sign a contract, and there would be witnesses

265
00:25:05,078 --> 00:25:06,516
some of the terms in the contract

266
00:25:06,619 --> 00:25:08,552
أَلَّا يَرْقَبْ بَرْضُوْنًاً

267
00:25:08,828 --> 00:25:16,324
Barzoon(برضون), is an animal, in terms of sizes between a donkey and a horse

268
00:25:17,643 --> 00:25:24,733
and it's expensive and it was used as a form of transportation for the elite.

269
00:25:26,387 --> 00:25:29,946
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) said: None of my governors are allowed to use that

270
00:25:31,098 --> 00:25:32,509
وَلَا يَعْكُلْ نَقِيًّا ,

271
00:25:32,708 --> 00:25:39,324
And they should not eat expensive food, nothing pure, nothing expensive.

272
00:25:39,978 --> 00:25:41,302
وَلَا يَلْبِسْ رَقِيْقًا ,

273
00:25:41,634 --> 00:25:44,059
And he should not wear soft clothes.

274
00:25:45,310 --> 00:25:51,074
So, if you had a suit and tie and fancy clothes on,

275
00:25:51,457 --> 00:25:52,894
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) would not like that.

276
00:25:56,042 --> 00:25:59,200
وَلَا يُغْلِقْ بَابَه’ دُوْنَ حَاجَتَ النَّاسْ,

277
00:25:59,834 --> 00:26:04,735
And you do not shut your door in front of any Muslim.

278
00:26:05,770 --> 00:26:11,685
Anyone who has a need you need to be ready and available to respond to their needs.

279
00:26:12,367 --> 00:26:15,417
So, his governors are really servants for the people.

280
00:26:25,198 --> 00:26:30,285
Number eight Shura(شورى) before he would choose a Waali(والي),

281
00:26:31,512 --> 00:26:34,651
he would consult with the seniors Sahabah(صحابه),

282
00:26:35,052 --> 00:26:36,887
Uthman Ibn Affan(عثمان ابن عفان), Ali Ibn Abi Talib(علي ابن ابي طالب),

283
00:26:36,912 --> 00:26:39,774
Abdur Rahman Bin Auf(عبدالرحمن ابن عوف), Az-Zubair Bin Awwam(ألزبيربن عوام)

284
00:26:40,192 --> 00:26:44,045
 these were his close advisors, Saad Bin Abi Waqas(سعدبن أبي وقاص)

285
00:26:44,457 --> 00:26:47,758
he would make Shura(شورى), before he would appoint anyone.

286
00:26:48,683 --> 00:26:50,097
Number nine;

287
00:26:51,200 --> 00:26:54,795
If he doesn't know the Waali(والي), first hand.

288
00:26:56,658 --> 00:26:58,304
He would test him,

289
00:26:59,979 --> 00:27:05,053
so he invited Al-Ahnaf Bin Qais(ألأخنف بن قيس) to come to Madina.

290
00:27:06,784 --> 00:27:09,204
So, Al-Ahnaf Bin Qais(ألأخنف بن قيس), comes in to Madina.

291
00:27:09,870 --> 00:27:11,909
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) holds him in Madina.

292
00:27:12,564 --> 00:27:15,810
Al-Ahnaf(ألأخنف), wants to leave and Umar(عُمَر) is holding him back.

293
00:27:17,698 --> 00:27:26,208
For a full year, He had him in Madina for a full year, after this year past.

294
00:27:27,425 --> 00:27:28,890
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب), told Al-Ahnaf(ألأخنف).

295
00:27:29,987 --> 00:27:37,365
يَا أَحْنَفْ قَدْ بَلَوْتُكَا وَ خَبِرْتُكَا فَرَاأَيْتُ أَنَّا عَلى نِيَّتَكَ حَسَنَا

296
00:27:38,058 --> 00:27:42,475
وَأَنَا أَرْجُوْ أَنْ تَكُوْنَ سَرِيْرَتَكَا مِثْلَعَنَا عَلى نِيَّتِكِ

297
00:27:43,234 --> 00:27:49,422
وَاِنَّا كُنَّا نَحَدَّثْ أَنَّا مَا يُحْلِقُ هَذَهِ لّْاُمَّهْ كُلَّا مُنَافِقٍ عَلِيْمَ

298
00:27:50,195 --> 00:27:57,752
 O Ahnaf(ألأخنف), I was testing you and I found out that what appears from you is good

299
00:27:58,672 --> 00:28:03,375
and I asked Allah that what is inside you is even better

300
00:28:04,488 --> 00:28:07,260
and O Ahnaf(ألأخنف)! We used to be told

301
00:28:07,776 --> 00:28:13,030
that the ones who will destroy this Ummah(امة) are the Knowledgeable Munafiqeen(منافقين).

302
00:28:14,103 --> 00:28:17,472
ثُمَّ قَالْ , يَا أحْنَفْ أَتَدْرِيْ لِمَا تَبَسْتُكْ

303
00:28:18,345 --> 00:28:22,210
And then he said: O Ahnaf(ألأخنف), Do you know why I held you back for a year?

304
00:28:22,915 --> 00:28:25,449
It is because I want to appoint you as a governor.

305
00:28:27,446 --> 00:28:32,697
So, he tested him, he would not rush to judgment, he was not spontaneous.

306
00:28:33,508 --> 00:28:37,141
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب), would not take a decision unless

307
00:28:37,227 --> 00:28:41,249
he knows exactly what he's doing, he wouldn't rush to judgment.

308
00:28:43,191 --> 00:28:48,070
Sometimes, we were very fast in making assumptions.

309
00:28:49,081 --> 00:28:51,964
We would see a person, we would immediately make a judgment on them

310
00:28:53,043 --> 00:28:55,410
even though our Farasah(فراسة) might be zero.

311
00:28:57,582 --> 00:28:59,859
Hear something on the news, immediately, make a judgment,

312
00:28:59,884 --> 00:29:02,214
read something in the paper, immediately make a judgment,

313
00:29:02,259 --> 00:29:03,743
No… you  know

314
00:29:03,918 --> 00:29:09,636
swallow it in, sit on it, think about it, don't just follow your whims your emotions.

315
00:29:11,225 --> 00:29:14,384
A Muslims should not rush into judgment

316
00:29:14,409 --> 00:29:19,892
especially when it is relating to information that is coming from a Fasiq(فاسق) source.

317
00:29:20,955 --> 00:29:25,030
يَا أَيُّهَا الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا إِنْ جَاءَكُمْ فَاسِقٌ بِنَبَإٍ فَتَبَيَّنُوا

318
00:29:26,256 --> 00:29:34,436
O you, who believe if a Fasiq(فاسق), a corrupt person and an untrustworthy person brings you some news verify it first.

319
00:29:35,007 --> 00:29:36,251
 Take the time to verify.

320
00:29:44,430 --> 00:29:45,581
Number Ten:

321
00:29:46,145 --> 00:29:52,375
 Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) would never allow himself or his governors

322
00:29:53,096 --> 00:29:57,820
to appoint non Muslims in any government responsibility.

323
00:29:58,344 --> 00:29:59,344
None!

324
00:29:59,716 --> 00:30:01,004
None, That  was a fixed rule.

325
00:30:03,243 --> 00:30:09,141
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب), was meeting with Abu Musa(أبوموسى).

326
00:30:11,973 --> 00:30:20,034
So, he told Abu Musa(أبوموسى): Have your assistant give the report in the Masjid(مسجد).

327
00:30:21,441 --> 00:30:24,184
Abu Musa(أبوموسى) said: He would not come into the Masjid(مسجد),

328
00:30:24,241 --> 00:30:26,093
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) said: How come?

329
00:30:26,569 --> 00:30:27,982
He said: Because he is Christian.

330
00:30:30,724 --> 00:30:32,740
This was an assistant of Abu Musa Al Ash'ari(ابوموسى ألأشعري),

331
00:30:33,497 --> 00:30:34,938
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) said;

332
00:30:36,841 --> 00:30:39,752
لَا تُدْنُوْ هُمْ,وَقَدْأَقْصَاهُمُ اللهَ

333
00:30:40,646 --> 00:30:45,534
Do not bring them close, when Allah has made them far away,

334
00:30:46,479 --> 00:30:48,489
when Allah has distanced them from you,

335
00:30:49,440 --> 00:30:51,732
وَلَا تُكْرِمُوْهُمْ وَقَدْ أَهَانَهُمُ اللهَ

336
00:30:52,111 --> 00:30:54,793
And do not honor them, when Allah has dishonored them.

337
00:30:55,743 --> 00:30:58,293
وَلَا تَأْمَنُوْ هُمْ وَقَدْ خَوَّ نُهُمُ اللهَ

338
00:30:58,587 --> 00:31:03,438
And do not trust them, when Allah has said that they are untrustworthy.

339
00:31:05,691 --> 00:31:12,013
And Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) he had a servant, his name is Ashiq(عأشِق),

340
00:31:13,504 --> 00:31:14,369
he said;

341
00:31:14,441 --> 00:31:21,494
كُنْتُ عَبْدًانَصْرَانِيًا لِعُمر, فَقَالَ: أَسْلِمْ حَتَّى نَسْتَعِيْنَ بِكَ عَلَى بَعْضِ أُمُوْرِ الْمُسْلِمِيْنَ

342
00:31:21,834 --> 00:31:25,959
لِأَنَّه’ لَا يَنْبَغِيْ لَنَا أَنْ نَسْتَعِيْنَ عَلَى أَمُوْرِهِمْ بِمَنْ لَيْسَ مِنْهُمْ

343
00:31:26,354 --> 00:31:29,660
 He told his Christian servant, I want you to become Muslim.

344
00:31:29,956 --> 00:31:35,429
So, that I can appoint you in some positions of responsibility

345
00:31:35,469 --> 00:31:39,907
because we are not allowed to seek assistance from non Muslims.

346
00:31:40,829 --> 00:31:45,113
Ashiq(عاشق) said: I told Umar(عُمَر): I don't want to change my religion.

347
00:31:45,712 --> 00:31:47,547
And Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) was fine with that. He said:

348
00:31:47,572 --> 00:31:48,316
لَاِ كْرَاهَا فِى الدِّيْنَ

349
00:31:48,364 --> 00:31:50,680
There's no compulsion in religion.

350
00:31:54,238 --> 00:31:59,126
Some of the characteristics of the men, whom umar ibn al-khattab رضي الله عنه chose.

351
00:31:59,667 --> 00:32:00,984
Number one: Az-Zuhad(الزهد),

352
00:32:02,142 --> 00:32:05,782
All of these men were austere, they had Az-Zuhad(الزهد),

353
00:32:06,160 --> 00:32:08,843
they were not attached to Duniyah(دُنِيَّا), they did not love Duniyah(دُنِيَّا).

354
00:32:10,160 --> 00:32:14,075
Therefore, this made them work for the sake of Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ, and for Aakhira(آخرة).

355
00:32:15,144 --> 00:32:17,663
They were not serving their personal interests.

356
00:32:18,347 --> 00:32:22,029
You know, even though all of them were Zuhaad(زهاد), but some of them

357
00:32:22,301 --> 00:32:26,387
were on an even higher level, such as Saeed Bin Amir(سعيد بن عامر),

358
00:32:28,087 --> 00:32:30,525
Abu Musa Al Ash'ari(ابوموسى ألأشعري), Muadh Ibn Jabal(معاذإبن جبل),

359
00:32:31,368 --> 00:32:35,866
Abu Obaidah Amr Bin Jarrah(أبوعبيدةعمروبن جراح), Salaman Al Farsi(سلمان الفارسي).

360
00:32:36,436 --> 00:32:39,867
These among, the Sahabah(صحابه) were famous as being Zuhaad(زهاد),

361
00:32:40,554 --> 00:32:45,385
all of the Sahabah(صحابه) were Zuhaad(زهاد), but these were even at a higher level.

362
00:32:46,087 --> 00:32:49,944
And these were all men whom Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) appointed as Wulaa(ولاه).

363
00:32:51,501 --> 00:32:55,742
Number two: They  were very humble and power did not changed them.

364
00:32:57,576 --> 00:33:03,254
They never changed their ways, the simple ways of the Arabs of Arabia.

365
00:33:05,599 --> 00:33:09,330
They carried on living a simple life,

366
00:33:10,827 --> 00:33:18,748
the Romans sent a representative to meet with the Muslim Ameer(أمير) of the armies in Ash-sham(ألشام)

367
00:33:19,454 --> 00:33:22,276
 and who was the Ameer(أمير), Abu Obaidah(ابوعبيدة),

368
00:33:23,610 --> 00:33:26,013
one of the 10 given the glad tidings of Jannah(جنة).

369
00:33:27,584 --> 00:33:30,718
So, this Roman representative is coming from a certain culture,

370
00:33:31,365 --> 00:33:37,534
where they treat, the leaders with certain respect,

371
00:33:38,073 --> 00:33:42,330
the way they dress is different, the way they sit is different, the way they act is different.

372
00:33:43,951 --> 00:33:47,168
So, he comes in and the Muslims are just sitting on the floor.

373
00:33:49,477 --> 00:33:51,174
He said: Where is your Ameer(أمير)?.

374
00:33:51,745 --> 00:33:53,858
So, they pointed towards Abu Obaidah(ابوعبيدة).

375
00:33:54,243 --> 00:33:55,707
He said: I came to a man

376
00:33:56,128 --> 00:33:57,128
متنكب القوس

377
00:33:57,493 --> 00:34:02,544
he was sitting on the floor with his bow on his shoulder,

378
00:34:03,093 --> 00:34:05,576
and he was playing with arrows in his hand.

379
00:34:07,290 --> 00:34:09,613
So, I came to him and I said;

380
00:34:09,802 --> 00:34:11,156
How come you're sitting on the floor?

381
00:34:11,196 --> 00:34:14,759
You know, Subhaan Allah(سُبْحَان الله), He came with a completely different mission

382
00:34:15,177 --> 00:34:19,232
but just he couldn't hold back asking Abu Obaidah(ابوعبيدة) this question.

383
00:34:19,257 --> 00:34:20,898
He said: How come you're sitting on the floor?

384
00:34:22,818 --> 00:34:25,931
Would it make you different in the eyes of Allah if you are sitting on a throne.

385
00:34:30,347 --> 00:34:34,558
Abu Obaidah رضي الله عنه said: I'm going to be very honest with you

386
00:34:34,583 --> 00:34:36,164
and I'm going to tell you the truth.

387
00:34:39,646 --> 00:34:45,042
 I have no dirham(درهم) or dinar(دينار) in my pocket, I am broke

388
00:34:47,301 --> 00:34:49,917
you know, imagine an Ameer(أمير) telling a representative here.

389
00:34:49,950 --> 00:34:55,203
And Abu Obaidah(ابوعبيدة) said: I'm going to tell you the truth, I have nothing I'm broke

390
00:34:56,121 --> 00:35:01,690
and I had to borrow money from my brother Muadh Ibn Jabal(معاذإبن جبل) to feed myself.

391
00:35:04,725 --> 00:35:12,896
But then he said: But even if I had money enough to buy for myself a throne to sit on.

392
00:35:14,396 --> 00:35:18,159
I'm not going to be a person, who would sit on the throne

393
00:35:18,938 --> 00:35:22,630
and have my Muslim brother sit under me on the floor,

394
00:35:23,172 --> 00:35:30,105
when he could be better in the eyes of Allah then myself, and then he said;

395
00:35:34,315 --> 00:35:39,805
وَنَحْنُ عِبَادَ الله نَمْشِيْ عَلَى الْأَرْضَ،وَ نَجْلِسُ عَلَى الْأَرْضَ،

396
00:35:40,405 --> 00:35:43,600
وَنَأْكُلُ عَلَى الْأَرْضَ، وَنَضَجِّعَ عَلَى الْأَرْضَ

397
00:35:43,856 --> 00:35:46,628
وَلَيْسَ ذَالِكَ يَنْقُصُنَا عِنْدِاللهِ شَيْئَا ،

398
00:35:46,900 --> 00:35:54,036
بَلْ يُعَظِّمَ اللهُ بِهِ أَجُوْ رَنَا ، وَيَرْفَعْدَرَجَاتِنَا، وَنَتَوَاضَعُ بِذَالِكَ لِرَبِّنَا

399
00:35:54,541 --> 00:35:59,961
And he said: And we the servants of Allah, we walk on the floor,

400
00:36:00,723 --> 00:36:07,041
and we sit on the floor, and we eat on the floor, and we sleep on the floor.

401
00:36:07,465 --> 00:36:10,272
And that does not reduce us in the eyes of Allah.

402
00:36:10,297 --> 00:36:14,439
In fact, it raises our status in the eyes of Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ.

403
00:36:20,975 --> 00:36:23,608
So, they're very humble, simple.

404
00:36:24,793 --> 00:36:35,071
And you know, that's a lesson for us, it is not your clothes that make you who you are?

405
00:36:35,331 --> 00:36:41,074
It's not the way you try to act, it's not the image that you try to project,

406
00:36:41,380 --> 00:36:47,638
it's not the car that you drive, it is what is in your heart.

407
00:36:50,022 --> 00:36:54,755
And sometimes when people put on a show, which is fake.

408
00:36:55,772 --> 00:36:59,226
Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ does not let them die, until he exposes them.

409
00:37:01,813 --> 00:37:09,270
So, we ask Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ to give us all Sitr(ستر), to conceal our privacy's

410
00:37:10,190 --> 00:37:13,165
and to make our Sareerah(سريره) better than Ala-niyah(اعلانيعة).

411
00:37:13,190 --> 00:37:15,334
To make the private better than the public.

412
00:37:17,784 --> 00:37:24,011
So, Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ honored these Sahabah(صحابه),

413
00:37:27,320 --> 00:37:30,621
but the honor that he gave them was not through the clothes that they were wearing

414
00:37:30,645 --> 00:37:34,297
or the Barzoon(برضون) that they were riding or the throne they were sitting on.

415
00:37:36,218 --> 00:37:43,638
Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ honored them by putting the love of them, in the hearts of the Aoulea(أوليآء) of Allah.

416
00:37:44,695 --> 00:37:47,182
Every Walli(ولي) of Allahعَزَّوَجَل loves Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب).

417
00:37:47,788 --> 00:37:51,846
Every Walli(ولي) of Allah loves Abu Obaidah(ابوعبيدة), even though Abu Obaidah(ابوعبيدة) would sit on the floor

418
00:37:53,632 --> 00:38:00,536
because the Sahabah رضي الله عنهم understood that it's not this position of Ameer(أمير) that would give him the status.

419
00:38:00,710 --> 00:38:04,046
 They understood, that Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ said in Qur'an;

420
00:38:04,071 --> 00:38:08,825
تُؤْتِي الْمُلْكَ مَنْ تَشَاءُ وَتَنْزِعُ الْمُلْكَ مِمَّنْ تَشَاءُ

421
00:38:09,629 --> 00:38:15,036
Allah gives kingdom to whomever, He wishes and He strips it away, from whoever He wishes.

422
00:38:16,168 --> 00:38:22,797
And a person could be in the utmost level of magnificence and strength and power

423
00:38:22,996 --> 00:38:29,742
and Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ can humiliate that person and bring him down to the lowest levels that can happen.

424
00:38:31,736 --> 00:38:34,404
Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ gives the kingdom to whomever He wills

425
00:38:34,729 --> 00:38:37,142
and He takes it away from whomever He wills.

426
00:38:39,538 --> 00:38:40,825
And Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ honors.

427
00:38:40,873 --> 00:38:42,997
وَتُعِزُّ مَنْ تَشَاءُ وَتُذِلُّ مَنْ تَشَاءُ

428
00:38:43,491 --> 00:38:48,515
And Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ honors whomever He wills and He humiliates, whoever He wills,

429
00:38:49,712 --> 00:38:53,761
and it's the destiny of Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ that He will honor the believers

430
00:38:54,305 --> 00:38:56,656
and He will dishonor the disbelievers

431
00:38:57,665 --> 00:39:00,781
and if that doesn't happen in Duniyah(دُنِيَّا) and it will happen one day,

432
00:39:00,973 --> 00:39:03,150
it will definitely happen on the Day of Judgment.

433
00:39:05,973 --> 00:39:10,057
Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ said in Qur'an and Rasool Allah ﷺ says it in the Hadith(حديث).

434
00:39:11,342 --> 00:39:16,130
Let the disbelievers do whatever they want, assume whatever power they want,

435
00:39:17,147 --> 00:39:18,833
gather all of the money they want.

436
00:39:19,474 --> 00:39:23,637
Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ will expose them and Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ put them in the place that they deserve.

437
00:39:25,180 --> 00:39:28,142
Everything is done in Duniyah(دُنِيَّا) is temporary and it will go.

438
00:39:29,235 --> 00:39:33,647
The money of Qaroon(قارون) did not last long and the kingdom of Firaun(فرعون) did not last long

439
00:39:34,259 --> 00:39:36,256
and Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ humiliated both of them. ?

440
00:39:37,437 --> 00:39:41,937
And the great humiliation for both of them will even be more on the day of judgment

441
00:39:41,962 --> 00:39:43,191
when they meet Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ

442
00:39:44,865 --> 00:39:49,377
and the believers who were dishonored in Duniyah(دُنِيَّا) and were persecuted and killed

443
00:39:49,779 --> 00:39:53,567
Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ has reserved from them, a very high status on the Day of Judgment.

444
00:39:54,740 --> 00:39:58,231
Just imagine what Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ will do to the people of Ukhdood(ألأخدود)

445
00:39:58,743 --> 00:40:01,203
The believers who are burnt alive in the trenches.

446
00:40:02,336 --> 00:40:05,913
How will Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ honor the Sahabah(صحابه) who died as Shuhadaa(شهداء)?

447
00:40:06,677 --> 00:40:09,235
How will Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ honor Hamza bin Abdul Mutalib(حمزةبن عبدالمطلب).?

448
00:40:12,060 --> 00:40:19,664
How will Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ honor the Qurr'aa(قراء) of Quran, who were executed by the disbelieving Arab tribes.

449
00:40:20,964 --> 00:40:24,100
Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ will hold them in very high status on the Day of Judgment.

450
00:40:25,244 --> 00:40:27,437
And that's when everybody will be jealous with that status.

451
00:40:27,461 --> 00:40:29,463
And they would have wish that they have followed that path.

452
00:40:31,684 --> 00:40:36,343
So, if you don't see justice in Duniyah(دُنِيَّا), if you see a lot of unfairness in Duniyah(دُنِيَّا).

453
00:40:37,992 --> 00:40:42,296
Don't be disheartened because the day of justice is the day of judgment

454
00:40:42,321 --> 00:40:44,063
and that's why it's called the Day of Judgment.

455
00:40:45,961 --> 00:40:50,390
It is the day of judgment…. It's a day of justice....

456
00:40:58,034 --> 00:41:00,665
They had Wara'a(وراع) piety

457
00:41:03,760 --> 00:41:08,292
and Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) had a problem with convincing some of them to be governors.

458
00:41:09,045 --> 00:41:13,083
Ut'ba Bin Ghazwaan(عتبة بن غزوآن), he came to Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) and said;

459
00:41:13,108 --> 00:41:14,982
I don't want to be the governor over Basra(بصرى).

460
00:41:15,507 --> 00:41:18,235
Find somebody else Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) refused.

461
00:41:19,751 --> 00:41:23,325
Ibn Abbas(إبن عباس) when the governor of Homs(حمص) died.

462
00:41:23,349 --> 00:41:28,062
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) tried to convince him to become the Waali(والي) over Hims.

463
00:41:28,290 --> 00:41:30,197
Ibn Abbas(إبن عباس) said: No way!

464
00:41:32,193 --> 00:41:35,319
I'm no Waali(والي), I'm not going to become a Waali(والي).

465
00:41:37,583 --> 00:41:41,157
Nauman Bin Maqran(نعمان بن مقرن), he comes to Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) and he said;

466
00:41:41,295 --> 00:41:44,070
Please discharge me from being a Waali(والي)

467
00:41:44,453 --> 00:41:46,836
because I want to go and fight Fee-Sabeel-Lillah(فِي سَبيل الله).

468
00:41:49,282 --> 00:41:52,082
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) came to Az-Zubair Bin Awwam(ألزبيربن عوام) and told him;

469
00:41:52,282 --> 00:42:01,423
You are my governor over Egypt - Egypt! The jewel, Egypt very important government, Wealthy and huge.

470
00:42:02,399 --> 00:42:04,725
 Zubair(زبير) you are my governor over Egypt.

471
00:42:05,271 --> 00:42:05,820
Zubair(زبير) said;

472
00:42:05,885 --> 00:42:09,825
لَا حَاجَةْ لِيْ فِيْهَا وَلَكِنْ أَخْرُجْ مُجَاهِدًا ولِلْمُسْلِمِيْنَ مُعَاوِناً

473
00:42:09,943 --> 00:42:12,006
I don't want to be a governor of the Egypt,

474
00:42:12,340 --> 00:42:15,980
I want to be Mujahid(مجاهد) Fee-Sabeel-Lillah(فِي سَبيل الله) and a helper of the Muslims.

475
00:42:19,098 --> 00:42:25,633
That was the life they wanted to live there are not looking into infiltrating governments and becoming leaders.

476
00:42:25,922 --> 00:42:30,157
They wanted to go Fee-Sabeel-Lillah(فِي سَبيل الله عَزَوَجَلّ) and die Fee-Sabeel-Lillah(فِي سَبيل الله)

477
00:42:30,395 --> 00:42:32,559
that was the path that they chose for themselves.

478
00:42:38,435 --> 00:42:43,077
THE RESPONSIBILITIES WULAA'A(ولآة).

479
00:42:43,513 --> 00:42:46,208
What were their responsibilities in those days?

480
00:42:47,038 --> 00:42:51,811
Number one, the most important responsibility is to establish the Deen(دِيْن) of Allah.

481
00:42:52,483 --> 00:42:53,614
اقامة دين

482
00:42:56,523 --> 00:43:00,220
Yazeed Ibn Abi Sufiyan(يزيدبن أبي سُفيان), he sends a letter to Ameer Ul-Mo'mineen(أميرالمؤمنين) and he said;

483
00:43:00,611 --> 00:43:07,722
إِنَّ اَهْلَ الشَّامِ قَدْ كَثَرُوْ وَمَلَاْءُ الْمَدَائِنَ وَحْتَاجُ اِلَى مَنْ يُعَلِّمُ هُمُ الْقُرْآنْ

484
00:43:07,929 --> 00:43:12,173
وَيُفَقِّهُّمْ  فَإِنِّيْ بِرِجَالٍ يُعَلِّمُوْنَھم

485
00:43:13,552 --> 00:43:19,692
Yazeed(يزيد) said: The people in the Ash-Sham(ألشام) have multiplied the population is increasing

486
00:43:20,422 --> 00:43:28,597
and they are filling the towns of Ash-Sham(ألشام), and they need men to teach them Qur'an.

487
00:43:29,231 --> 00:43:32,430
So, help me with men who would teach them.

488
00:43:33,043 --> 00:43:36,712
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) sent him five of the Fuqahaa(فقهاء) of Sahabah(صحابه).

489
00:43:39,770 --> 00:43:43,004
They were very short, the Sahabah(صحابه) were very short in manpower

490
00:43:43,029 --> 00:43:46,133
because the number of the Sahabah(صحابه) was very low.

491
00:43:50,649 --> 00:43:55,676
Nevertheless, Subhaan Allah(سُبْحَان الله), the lands that were opened by the Sahabah(صحابه)

492
00:43:59,032 --> 00:44:07,136
are the lands in which not only Islam took root but the Arabic language also flourished.

493
00:44:08,658 --> 00:44:11,182
Unlike the lands that were opened after the Sahabah(صحابه).

494
00:44:13,514 --> 00:44:17,655
In Ash-Sham(ألشام) you have some Arab tribes living but not all of Ash-Sham(ألشام) were Arabs.

495
00:44:17,680 --> 00:44:21,669
Syria, Jordan, Lebanon and Falastine(فلسطين) not all of the people were Arabs.

496
00:44:21,694 --> 00:44:26,323
You have a lot of indigenous Roman people, the Arabs were scattered tribes

497
00:44:26,853 --> 00:44:31,125
but nowadays that's the official language of out of these four countries i.e. Arabic.

498
00:44:31,775 --> 00:44:33,204
No other languages exist.

499
00:44:33,658 --> 00:44:39,579
Egypt was a non Arab country, they were Coptic's and they had their own language.

500
00:44:40,136 --> 00:44:43,524
Now, the Egyptians have adopted Arabic language and they became Arabs.

501
00:44:44,709 --> 00:44:52,599
North Africa, you had the barber people and then some Arab tribes settled

502
00:44:53,019 --> 00:44:58,010
in Algeria, Tunisia, Morocco and Libya.

503
00:44:58,866 --> 00:45:02,002
However, all of these countries now speak Arabic.

504
00:45:03,155 --> 00:45:07,681
Al-Andalus(ألأندلس) also for 800 years the language was Arabic.

505
00:45:11,478 --> 00:45:14,751
While you would find that in the time of a Taba'een(تابعين) and Taba Taba'een(تابع تابعين)

506
00:45:14,776 --> 00:45:19,413
Islam would take root but the language didn't go beyond that area.

507
00:45:20,098 --> 00:45:25,232
So, even though the Sahabah رضي الله عنهم were very short on the human resources

508
00:45:25,543 --> 00:45:27,460
but Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ blessed their efforts.

509
00:45:29,024 --> 00:45:33,907
Subhaan Allah(سُبْحَان الله), we can't even imagine how much Hasanaat(حسانات) are being piled up

510
00:45:34,397 --> 00:45:39,346
on the scales of the Sahabah رضي الله عنهم on the DAY of JUDGEMENT

511
00:45:41,779 --> 00:45:44,195
because, it goes to their credit that we are Muslim today.

512
00:45:45,282 --> 00:45:47,227
They are to be credited with that.!

513
00:45:48,656 --> 00:45:52,822
So, everything that we do, they receive a copy of that in their account.

514
00:46:01,799 --> 00:46:05,305
In the time of Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب), he built about 4000 Masajid(مساجد).

515
00:46:09,369 --> 00:46:12,552
Number two: Tamaeen an-Naas(تعمين الناس),

516
00:46:13,957 --> 00:46:17,948
Providing peace and security to their subjects.

517
00:46:19,841 --> 00:46:24,378
They would guard them, they would protect them, so peace flourished.

518
00:46:25,312 --> 00:46:31,465
A Muslim could leave their shop unlocked and go to Salah(صلاة),

519
00:46:34,408 --> 00:46:38,267
A Muslim woman can go out and travel fearing no one.

520
00:46:39,025 --> 00:46:42,934
Rasool Allah ﷺ said, in the Hadith(حديث) to Udae Bin Hatim(عدي بن حاتم)

521
00:46:44,924 --> 00:46:50,164
تَخْرُجُ ازَّعِيْنَهْ مِنْ أَلْهِيْرَهْ إِلَي مَكَّهْ

522
00:46:50,660 --> 00:46:56,714
A woman would come all the way from Iraq to Makkah, fearing no one but Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ.

523
00:47:01,418 --> 00:47:04,150
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) he sent a letter to Abu Musa Al-Ash'ari(أبوموسى ألأشعري), He said:

524
00:47:04,188 --> 00:47:05,880
اَخيف لفسّاقأ

525
00:47:08,688 --> 00:47:11,421
Put fear in the hearts of the evil doers,

526
00:47:12,604 --> 00:47:20,928
the Fussaaq(فساق) the burglars, the Raiders, the gangs, strike fear in their hearts.

527
00:47:23,026 --> 00:47:25,585
Make them think twice before they commit any crime.

528
00:47:26,729 --> 00:47:31,062
By applying the Hudood(حدود) of Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ, that's how they establish security for the people.

529
00:47:33,809 --> 00:47:37,045
Number three, Al-Jihad(جهاد) Fee-Sabeel-Lillah(فِي سَبيل الله).

530
00:47:37,460 --> 00:47:43,770
It was the responsibility of the Wullaa(ولأء) to establish this great Shaeera(شعيره) of Islam

531
00:47:44,296 --> 00:47:45,828
Al-Jihad(جهاد) Fee-Sabeel-Lillah(فِي سَبيل الله)

532
00:47:46,242 --> 00:47:49,295
and their roles involved Irsaal Al-Mutatawieen(إرسال ألمتتوعين),

533
00:47:49,683 --> 00:47:55,166
sending the volunteers they would organize recruitment in the Masajid(مساجد),

534
00:47:55,358 --> 00:47:56,862
they would be recruited in the Masajid(مساجد).

535
00:47:57,803 --> 00:48:02,022
The Imam(اِمَام) would stand up and recruit them and then all of these recruits

536
00:48:02,405 --> 00:48:06,760
would go in and join in the camps and it is the responsibility of the Waalii(والي)

537
00:48:07,251 --> 00:48:09,590
to send them, where they are needed.

538
00:48:12,345 --> 00:48:18,368
Number 2, Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) has promised his people, he Said;

539
00:48:18,400 --> 00:48:21,411
وَلَكُمْ إِلَيَّ أَنْ أَسُدَّ صُغُرَكُمْ

540
00:48:22,384 --> 00:48:25,178
I promise you, to protect your borders.

541
00:48:26,618 --> 00:48:30,250
So, that was the responsibility of the Wullaa(وُلأء) on the frontier lands

542
00:48:30,564 --> 00:48:34,187
to protect the borders from any attacks by the Kuffar(كفار).

543
00:48:35,220 --> 00:48:38,937
Number three Al-Tahseen(ألتّحسين) the building of fortresses,

544
00:48:39,238 --> 00:48:43,864
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) told Amr Bin Al-Aas(عَمْرُو بِن اَلْعَاص) to build fortresses in Al-Jesa(ألجيزة)

545
00:48:44,724 --> 00:48:47,506
because in Egypt, it was on the Mediterranean Sea.

546
00:48:47,665 --> 00:48:49,536
 So, it could be attacked by the Roman ships.

547
00:48:49,850 --> 00:48:52,039
So, he wanted them to build fortresses.

548
00:48:53,483 --> 00:48:59,400
Number 4. Intelligence it was the responsibility of the Wullaa(وُلأء)

549
00:48:59,600 --> 00:49:02,238
to gather intelligence information for the Khalifah(خليفة).

550
00:49:02,850 --> 00:49:07,367
We know that Abu Obaidah(ابوعبيدة) for example, He had many of the Muslims

551
00:49:07,792 --> 00:49:10,992
working in gathering intelligence for him,

552
00:49:11,105 --> 00:49:14,878
and then he would send that information to Umar Bin Khattab  رضي الله عنه.

553
00:49:15,166 --> 00:49:24,985
Number five. He also Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) asked the Wullaa(ولأء) to raise horses.

554
00:49:25,650 --> 00:49:33,980
So, they would have these pasture lands and they would raise in them hundreds of horses

555
00:49:34,972 --> 00:49:38,811
and these horses are for nothing but Al-Jihad(جهاد) Fee-Sabeel-Lillah(فِي سَبيل الله),

556
00:49:39,081 --> 00:49:40,787
they would not be used for anything else.

557
00:49:42,253 --> 00:49:47,753
So, for example you had in Al-Basra(ألبصره) actually I did read the numbers.

558
00:49:47,778 --> 00:49:49,062
I just didn't bring them with me.

559
00:49:49,149 --> 00:49:51,427
The number of horses in Al-Basra(ألبصره) and Al-Kufa(ألكوفه)

560
00:49:51,651 --> 00:49:55,635
and these were devoted for that cause and it was the responsibility of the Waali(والي)

561
00:49:55,931 --> 00:50:00,014
and he would appoint some men full time to take care of these ranchers.

562
00:50:06,657 --> 00:50:09,987
Number six: The training of the youth

563
00:50:11,256 --> 00:50:15,522
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) ordered that training camps would be opened in every Wulaaya(ولاية).

564
00:50:15,905 --> 00:50:26,177
To train the young, in target shooting, in swimming and in horseback riding

565
00:50:26,509 --> 00:50:30,804
in these three areas and even though there was a safety hazard

566
00:50:31,571 --> 00:50:35,417
and a report came to Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) that one of these young men died,

567
00:50:35,503 --> 00:50:38,753
in training that did not change a thing.

568
00:50:38,820 --> 00:50:39,754
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) said;

569
00:50:39,778 --> 00:50:42,916
That it should still carry on, even though somebody died.

570
00:50:44,021 --> 00:50:48,855
The training should still go on because this is Fee-Sabeel-Lillah(فِي سَبيل الله).

571
00:50:51,849 --> 00:50:57,197
They would be responsible for the financing of the armies and the paying of the salaries

572
00:50:57,574 --> 00:51:03,444
to the soldiers and they would also be involved in the negotiation and agreement with the enemies,

573
00:51:03,541 --> 00:51:11,721
 so that was number three

574
00:51:12,215 --> 00:51:14,947
Number four,

575
00:51:17,203 --> 00:51:22,389
They will try their best to provide sustenance for the people, Ar-Rizq(رزق).

576
00:51:25,436 --> 00:51:27,292
Al-Bayhaqi(ألبيهقي) narrates;

577
00:51:27,601 --> 00:51:30,931
أَنَّا عمر أَنْفَقَا عَلَى أَهْلِ ارَّمَادَهْ حَتَّي وَقَعَ ألْمَتَرْ

578
00:51:32,174 --> 00:51:38,250
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) carried on providing for the Bedouins in the refugee camps,

579
00:51:38,320 --> 00:51:39,321
 we talked about them.

580
00:51:39,681 --> 00:51:42,709
The Bedouins in the refugee camps that came to Madina.

581
00:51:43,256 --> 00:51:46,880
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) carried on spending on them

582
00:51:47,256 --> 00:51:55,401
until Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ, elevated the famine of Aam-Er-Ramadah(عام ألرمادة) and rain started falling down

583
00:51:56,127 --> 00:52:01,194
and that is when they started going back to their lands.

584
00:52:01,564 --> 00:52:03,913
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب), Al-Bayhaqi(ألبيهقي) said;

585
00:52:04,042 --> 00:52:09,448
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) went on his horse to witness the refugees,

586
00:52:09,503 --> 00:52:12,843
when they were leaving Madina and going back to their homes

587
00:52:13,785 --> 00:52:17,611
and it was said that tears started rolling down the cheeks of Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب).

588
00:52:18,802 --> 00:52:20,639
So, one man from Muharib(محارب) said;

589
00:52:21,734 --> 00:52:25,224
the famine of Ar-Ramada(ألرمادة) was elevated because of you.

590
00:52:26,170 --> 00:52:27,116
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) said;

591
00:52:27,141 --> 00:52:33,577
وَيْحَكْ ذَالِكَ لَوْ أَنْفَقْتَ مِنْ مَّالِيْ أَوْ مِنْ مَّالِ الْخَطَّابْ إِنَّمَا أَنْفَقْتُ مِّنْ مَّالِ الله

592
00:52:34,165 --> 00:52:37,812
Woe to you, you can say that if I spent from my own pocket

593
00:52:38,282 --> 00:52:40,433
or from the money of Al-Khattab(ألخطاب) from my father

594
00:52:40,853 --> 00:52:42,749
but I was spending from the money of Allah.

595
00:52:44,402 --> 00:52:47,407
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) was very emotional when he saw these refugees,

596
00:52:48,793 --> 00:52:55,432
bringing their children and their women and they were all going on their camels and leaving the refugee camps.

597
00:52:56,065 --> 00:52:59,553
Where they stayed there for months and months and months, suffering hunger.

598
00:52:59,710 --> 00:53:01,177
many of them died.

599
00:53:01,597 --> 00:53:06,353
And it was Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) as we talked earlier, he would cook for them, serve them, help them

600
00:53:06,694 --> 00:53:11,190
 and now Al-Hamdolillah(ألحمدلله) the problem was over and they're going back to their territories.

601
00:53:18,066 --> 00:53:23,332
Bilal رضي الله عنه was one of the zuhaad(زهاد) and Bilal(بلال) was very concerned with

602
00:53:23,614 --> 00:53:27,842
See! Some people they are austere in themselves, some people they want to be austere

603
00:53:27,919 --> 00:53:29,389
and they want everybody else to be austere.

604
00:53:30,223 --> 00:53:31,691
Bilal(بلال) was one of those people.

605
00:53:32,064 --> 00:53:37,677
Bilal(بلال) was very worried that the Muslim Ummah(امة) would become soft and luxurious.

606
00:53:38,521 --> 00:53:42,195
So, he comes to Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) to complain about what's happening in Syria.

607
00:53:42,732 --> 00:53:44,197
He came to Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) and he said;

608
00:53:44,607 --> 00:53:51,163
يَا أمير المؤمنين إِنَّ أُلمَّرَآ أَجْنَادَكَ بِشَّامِ وَاللهِ مَا يَاكُلُوْنَا إِلَّا هُمُّ طَّيْرَ

609
00:53:51,432 --> 00:53:54,804
وَخَبْزًا نَقِيْ وَمَا يِجِدُوْ ذَالِكَ عَامَّةِ الْمُسْلِمِيْنَ

610
00:53:55,428 --> 00:53:59,746
 O Ameer Ul-Mo'mineen(أميرالمؤمنين), your military generals in Ash-Sham(ألشام)

611
00:54:00,187 --> 00:54:08,380
are eating the flesh of birds, chicken and different fowl and they are eating soft bread.

612
00:54:10,169 --> 00:54:12,692
While that is not accessible to the rest of the Muslims.

613
00:54:13,051 --> 00:54:15,759
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) said: Bring them, call them.

614
00:54:16,513 --> 00:54:18,919
So, they came to Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) and he said;

615
00:54:18,944 --> 00:54:22,354
Is what Bilal(بلال) is claiming is that true.?

616
00:54:23,073 --> 00:54:24,442
Yazeed Bin Abi Sufiyaan(يزيدبن أبي سفيان) said;

617
00:54:24,474 --> 00:54:33,146
O Ameer Ul-Mo'mineen(أميرالمؤمنين), what Bilal(بلال) is saying about the food that we eat is true.

618
00:54:34,104 --> 00:54:37,615
But that is because it is very cheap in our land.

619
00:54:38,306 --> 00:54:45,592
And it costs the same as it would cost to feed our families in Al-Hijaz(ألحجاز).

620
00:54:46,548 --> 00:54:50,430
We are spending the same amount of money, we would be spending, if we are in Madina,

621
00:54:51,839 --> 00:54:55,568
we are buying these items because in this land, they're very cheap.

622
00:54:56,769 --> 00:55:03,309
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) said: Not until I make sure that you provide for your people.

623
00:55:04,107 --> 00:55:08,212
So, he brought the people and he said: What would be enough food for you in a month.

624
00:55:08,678 --> 00:55:14,754
So, they said: So and So bread and So and So vinegar and So and So olive oil.

625
00:55:15,172 --> 00:55:16,501
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) said;

626
00:55:17,445 --> 00:55:20,840
We write an agreement between you and your Governor's,

627
00:55:21,188 --> 00:55:23,842
that they will provide you with that amount of food.

628
00:55:25,425 --> 00:55:28,468
In addition to the handouts that the government gives.

629
00:55:30,245 --> 00:55:37,243
And if they do not fulfill that, you come and raise your complaints to me,

630
00:55:37,671 --> 00:55:41,810
and I will make sure that they will give you, what is due to you?

631
00:55:43,101 --> 00:55:46,304
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) did not allow his governors to eat soft bread.

632
00:55:46,621 --> 00:55:51,386
Until he made sure that everyone in Ash-Sham(ألشام) is going with a full stomach

633
00:55:51,411 --> 00:55:53,293
everyone has enough for them.

634
00:56:00,208 --> 00:56:10,004
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) wanted the governor's to seek Shuraa(شورى) from the seniors and the experienced.

635
00:56:10,363 --> 00:56:16,089
He heard that Abu Musa Al-Ash'ari(أبوموسى ألأشعرى) has an open door policy, when it comes to Shuraa(شورى)

636
00:56:16,462 --> 00:56:18,284
 anybody can come in and attend the Shuraa(شورى).

637
00:56:19,733 --> 00:56:24,486
The young, the old, the educated, the illiterate everyone.

638
00:56:25,195 --> 00:56:26,610
So, Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) told him;

639
00:56:27,754 --> 00:56:30,891
بَلَغَنِيْ أَنَّكَ تَعْزَنُ الِّنَّاسِ جَمًّا غَفِيْراً

640
00:56:30,923 --> 00:56:36,667
فَإِذَاجَآءَكَ كِتَابِ هَذَا فَعْزَنْ لِأَهْلِ الشَّرَفِيْ وَأَهْلِ الْقُرْآنَ وَتَّقْوَى وَدِّيْنَ

641
00:56:37,003 --> 00:56:39,597
فَإِذَا أَخَذُوْ مَجَالِسَ هُمْ فَعْزَنْ لِلْعَامَّهْ

642
00:56:39,691 --> 00:56:43,619
He said: Open your doors first to the leaders of the people

643
00:56:44,671 --> 00:56:46,670
and to the knowledgeable people,

644
00:56:46,924 --> 00:56:51,559
the people who are knowledgeable in Qur'an, and Islam.

645
00:56:52,931 --> 00:56:56,523
Let them come in first and take their seats.

646
00:56:57,127 --> 00:57:02,529
And then if there any other seats vacant, allow the rest to come in.

647
00:57:03,652 --> 00:57:06,855
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) is saying that when it comes to Shura(شورى),

648
00:57:07,629 --> 00:57:13,439
you should seek Shuraa(شورى), consultation with the leaders, with the scholars,

649
00:57:13,770 --> 00:57:17,197
with the people of experience, they should come in first,

650
00:57:17,393 --> 00:57:21,740
don't just open the doors and have everybody come into your Shuraa(شورى).

651
00:57:27,946 --> 00:57:33,573
And, you know, not only in Shuraa(شورى) is that the case

652
00:57:33,653 --> 00:57:44,841
but also in choosing leaders, electing leaders, it applies both to Shuraa(شورى) and the electing of leaders.

653
00:57:44,880 --> 00:57:48,990
It needs to be done by the people of experience and knowledge.

654
00:57:50,236 --> 00:57:51,672
 And he told Abu Musa(ابوموسى);

655
00:57:51,866 --> 00:57:57,817
لَمْ يَزَلِلنَّاسِ وُجُوْهُ يَرْفَعُوْنَ هَوَاءِجَالنَّاسِ فَأَكْرِمُوْ وَجُوْهَالنَّاسْ

656
00:57:58,179 --> 00:58:03,715
He said: People have leaders who represent them in asking for their needs

657
00:58:04,127 --> 00:58:05,494
so honor these people.

658
00:58:06,728 --> 00:58:14,521
In the tribal societies the tribe would have leaders and these leaders would go to the Sultan(سلطان)

659
00:58:15,468 --> 00:58:19,742
and ask help for his people.

660
00:58:20,393 --> 00:58:22,493
So, and so needs this, so and so needs that…

661
00:58:23,439 --> 00:58:27,360
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) is saying: Honor these people who are helping others.

662
00:58:30,954 --> 00:58:35,290
The governors of Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) used to be very caring,

663
00:58:36,092 --> 00:58:38,080
not only would they apply justice.

664
00:58:38,365 --> 00:58:41,555
You know?. You could apply justice in a very dry way and stay away from people.

665
00:58:42,115 --> 00:58:46,186
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) wanted them to show compassion, - not to show… To feel compassion.

666
00:58:46,274 --> 00:58:49,307
 It's not a show to feel compassion and to be caring

667
00:58:50,564 --> 00:58:54,844
about the subjects just like a shepherd would care about his flock.

668
00:58:55,874 --> 00:58:59,706
So, when he would meet with the followers with the people

669
00:59:00,390 --> 00:59:03,483
he would ask them, How is your Waali(والي)?

670
00:59:03,882 --> 00:59:07,037
They would say he's an excellent man! May Allah reward him.

671
00:59:07,616 --> 00:59:08,475
He would say;

672
00:59:09,321 --> 00:59:10,757
هَلْ يَعُوْضُوْ مَرْضَاكُمْ؟

673
00:59:11,462 --> 00:59:13,218
Does he visit your ill?

674
00:59:14,197 --> 00:59:15,361
هَلْ يَعُوْضُوْ الْعَبْدَ؟

675
00:59:15,994 --> 00:59:17,768
Does he visit the slave?

676
00:59:18,707 --> 00:59:20,419
كَيْفَ صَنْعِيَ أَوْ بِضَعِيُفَ؟

677
00:59:20,590 --> 00:59:22,323
How does he deal with the weak?

678
00:59:23,066 --> 00:59:24,601
هَلْ يَجْلِسُ عَلَى بَابْ؟

679
00:59:24,879 --> 00:59:28,207
Does he sit on the doorstep of the layman?

680
00:59:29,031 --> 00:59:31,600
If they answer no, to any of these questions.

681
00:59:31,909 --> 00:59:32,870
He would fire him.

682
00:59:35,062 --> 00:59:39,805
He needs to visit the ill and he needs to visit the slaves

683
00:59:40,742 --> 00:59:43,610
 and he needs to be kind with the weak.

684
00:59:46,223 --> 00:59:48,276
So, it goes beyond being just.

685
00:59:48,594 --> 00:59:50,824
You could be just without visiting the weak.

686
00:59:52,176 --> 00:59:58,224
But he wants them to care about their subjects and to be close to them.

687
01:00:01,348 --> 01:00:06,735
The governors of Umar(عُمَر) would ensure that people are treated equally.

688
01:00:06,759 --> 01:00:08,529
Once Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) was told:

689
01:00:09,148 --> 01:00:13,037
That one of his governors gave government handouts

690
01:00:13,132 --> 01:00:15,271
this money that the government would give to the subjects,

691
01:00:15,334 --> 01:00:17,924
he gave it to the Arabs and he didn't give it to the non Arabs.

692
01:00:18,814 --> 01:00:21,096
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) summoned him and he said;

693
01:00:22,705 --> 01:00:25,190
Why haven't you treated the people equally?

694
01:00:25,706 --> 01:00:32,205
People need to be treated equally the days of nationalism and tribalism are over.

695
01:00:36,593 --> 01:00:41,717
And Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) would follow up with his Wulaa(ولاء).

696
01:00:42,436 --> 01:00:43,650
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) said;

697
01:00:44,843 --> 01:00:49,927
خَيْرُ الِّيْ أَنْ أَعْزِلَ كُلَّ يَوْمٍ وَآلِيًا مِنْ أَنْ أُبْقِيْ ظَالِمًا سَاعَتْ أَنْهَارْ

698
01:00:50,033 --> 01:00:53,493
I would rather change the governor every day,

699
01:00:53,891 --> 01:00:57,523
then have a governor stay and oppress the people for one hour.

700
01:00:59,611 --> 01:01:05,671
Even if I would have to change him on a daily basis

701
01:01:07,104 --> 01:01:11,596
and cause all of that fluctuation and instability is better

702
01:01:11,854 --> 01:01:14,912
than having a Wali(والي), who is oppressing the people for even one hour.

703
01:01:15,364 --> 01:01:16,764
He used to say:

704
01:01:16,800 --> 01:01:22,176
أَيُّ مِنْ عَامِ الِّيْ ظَلَمَ اَحَدًا فَبَلَغَنِيْ مَظْلَمَتَا فَلَمْ أُغَيَّرَهَا فَأَنْ أَظْلَمْتَا

705
01:01:22,875 --> 01:01:28,222
 If I appoint a governor and then that Governor wrongs the people

706
01:01:28,688 --> 01:01:32,325
and I know about that then I have wronged them myself

707
01:01:34,222 --> 01:01:35,145
and he would say;

708
01:01:35,268 --> 01:01:39,435
أَرَأَيْتُ مِنَّ اسْتَعْمَلْتُ عَلَيْكُمْ خَيْرُ مَنْ اَعْلَمْ

709
01:01:39,776 --> 01:01:44,268
ثُمَّ أَمَرْتُه’ بِلْ عَدْلِ أَكُنْتُ قَضَيْتُمَا عَلَيْهِ فَقَالُ نَعْمَ

710
01:01:44,489 --> 01:01:50,085
 He asked the people he said: If I appoint on you, somebody who is good, pious

711
01:01:50,997 --> 01:01:57,161
and he is the best and I instruct him to rule with justice.

712
01:01:57,542 --> 01:01:58,819
Have I done my part.?

713
01:01:58,983 --> 01:02:00,058
They said: Definitely.

714
01:02:00,772 --> 01:02:03,213
You appointed somebody who is the best

715
01:02:03,655 --> 01:02:06,534
 and you instructed him to be just, you have done your part.

716
01:02:06,907 --> 01:02:08,184
He said: No! I haven't.

717
01:02:09,061 --> 01:02:14,596
قَالَ لَا، حَتَّى أَنْظُرَفِيْ عَمَلِيْهِ أَعَمِلَ بِمَا أَمَرْتَه’ عَمْلَا

718
01:02:14,866 --> 01:02:15,551
No,

719
01:02:16,115 --> 01:02:20,083
I would not have fulfilled my part until I follow up with him.

720
01:02:20,588 --> 01:02:25,718
And I put him under scrutiny to make sure that he is ruling according to what I instructed him.

721
01:02:26,563 --> 01:02:29,379
So, not only should I appoint the good but I need to follow up.

722
01:02:35,401 --> 01:02:37,620
When he would appoint a governor.

723
01:02:37,993 --> 01:02:46,998
He would ask that the people send the delegation to meet with him on a continuous basis,

724
01:02:47,642 --> 01:02:51,782
so that he can ask them about the Ummal(عُمَّالْ).

725
01:02:52,940 --> 01:02:56,341
So, he would receive a delegation of 10 from Al-Kufa(ألكوفه)

726
01:02:57,438 --> 01:03:01,375
and when the money from Al-Kufa(ألكوفه) would come

727
01:03:01,415 --> 01:03:05,858
and this money is the Kharaaj(خراج) and the Jizya(جزيه) and the Zakat(زكواة).

728
01:03:06,769 --> 01:03:11,952
He would instruct that this money needs to be accompanied by 10 representatives of the people.

729
01:03:12,980 --> 01:03:16,536
When he would receive the money who would ask these representatives. He would say:

730
01:03:17,441 --> 01:03:23,250
Do you testify that this money was taken in accordance to the laws of Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ

731
01:03:23,672 --> 01:03:26,746
and that no Muslim or non Muslim was wronged.

732
01:03:28,093 --> 01:03:30,049
When they would say yes, he would accept the money.

733
01:03:31,370 --> 01:03:36,322
He didn't want, one Dirham(درهم) to be taken unlawfully from a Muslim or non Muslim

734
01:03:37,596 --> 01:03:40,952
and he had to make sure that there are Shuhood(شهود), ten witnesses

735
01:03:41,257 --> 01:03:43,529
to ensure that this money was taken in the right way.

736
01:03:48,069 --> 01:03:56,379
He would have Baraid(بريد) a mail, the mail man would gather all of the letters

737
01:03:56,776 --> 01:03:58,705
and he would announce his departure date.

738
01:04:00,952 --> 01:04:05,705
And he would gather all of the letters and he would not be allowed to read any of them.

739
01:04:07,268 --> 01:04:11,958
And the mail would be delivered to Ameer Ul-Mo'mineen(أميرالمؤمنين) in Madina.

740
01:04:12,323 --> 01:04:14,830
So, if anyone had a private complain,

741
01:04:15,473 --> 01:04:18,727
they could write it down and send it to the Khalifah(خليفه) without even traveling

742
01:04:19,770 --> 01:04:23,217
and no one, would have read that mail.

743
01:04:26,788 --> 01:04:32,645
It's not like that the Waali(والي) has a right to peek into those envelopes

744
01:04:34,015 --> 01:04:39,589
based on intelligence information that he is complaining against you.

745
01:04:40,097 --> 01:04:44,716
The Privacy was secured, whatever was written is private,

746
01:04:45,009 --> 01:04:48,431
only the Khalifah(خليفه) will read it.

747
01:04:49,190 --> 01:04:51,790
He used to take advantage of the Hajj(حَجْ).

748
01:04:52,772 --> 01:04:54,207
Hajj(حَجْ) was a general assembly.

749
01:04:54,247 --> 01:04:59,866
You know? Now Hajj(حَجْ) today is devoid of its role.

750
01:05:00,369 --> 01:05:05,574
In the time of Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) Hajj(حَجْ) was a general assembly.

751
01:05:07,017 --> 01:05:09,680
Where he would ask the people about their governors,

752
01:05:10,234 --> 01:05:18,958
it was a Shura(شورى) for Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) to meet with his employees.

753
01:05:19,983 --> 01:05:23,250
It was a time to plan for the next year,

754
01:05:24,329 --> 01:05:30,303
 it was a time to report what is happening in every Muslim state to the Khalifah(خليفه).

755
01:05:31,889 --> 01:05:37,276
It was a time to hold the leaders accountable to the followers.

756
01:05:37,561 --> 01:05:40,880
That was the role of Hajj(حَجْ) in the time of Umar Bin Khattab رضي الله عنه.

757
01:05:45,016 --> 01:05:47,553
 Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) he said;

758
01:05:47,712 --> 01:05:52,124
لَإِنْ إِشْتُ إِنْ شَاءَاللهُ لَا أَسِيْرَنَّا فِى رَّعِيَّتِ حَوْلَا

759
01:05:53,074 --> 01:05:54,765
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) said: If I live,

760
01:05:55,495 --> 01:06:00,232
I am going to travel for a whole year to the different Muslim states.

761
01:06:01,420 --> 01:06:04,314
فَإِنِّيْ أَعْلَمُوْأَنَّا لِا لنَّاسِ حَوَائِجْ تُكْتَ عَدُوْنِيْ

762
01:06:05,747 --> 01:06:11,009
Because I'm sure that the people have needs and they're unable to deliver the request to me.

763
01:06:13,336 --> 01:06:17,793
إِمَّا عُمَّالَهُمْ فَلَا إِدْفَعُوْنَ اِلَيْهِ فَإِمَّالَهُمْ لَايَسِلُوْنَ اِلَيْهِ

764
01:06:18,086 --> 01:06:22,305
Either their leaders are not bringing those demands forth,

765
01:06:22,648 --> 01:06:24,863
or they are not able to send them to me.

766
01:06:25,844 --> 01:06:28,363
فَا أَسِيْرَ إِلَّى الشَّامْ فَأُقِيْمَ بِهَا شَهْرَيْنَ

767
01:06:28,946 --> 01:06:31,630
 So, I would go to Ash-Sham(ألشام) and stay two months.

768
01:06:32,233 --> 01:06:34,854
ثُمَّ أَسِيْرُ إِلَى الْجَزِيْرَهْ فَأُقِيْمُ بِهَا شَهْرَيْنَ

769
01:06:35,108 --> 01:06:37,422
And then I would go to Iraq and stay for two months

770
01:06:37,640 --> 01:06:39,858
and then to Al-Kufa(ألكوفه) and I would stay two months

771
01:06:40,139 --> 01:06:41,854
and then also to Al-Basra(ألبصرة) and stay two months.

772
01:06:42,832 --> 01:06:46,757
So, he wanted to go around traveling in order to ensure that

773
01:06:46,789 --> 01:06:54,353
every Muslim, every citizen of the Islamic Khilafah(خِلَافَه) has his needs fulfilled.

774
01:06:54,634 --> 01:06:58,657
IT SHUDDERS IN PAIN FREELY

775
01:06:58,803 --> 01:07:02,971
MY CHASITY, MY MODESTY!

776
01:07:03,061 --> 01:07:07,269
OH MUSLIM, YOU SAW

777
01:07:07,359 --> 01:07:11,535
MY INJURY AND THE INJURY OF MY PRIDE

